Local patch 0008 (qwen3.8-flash-next-exl3-tensorfold): the prompt cache's host copies off the GPU's path.

Why: 0006 copied each saved point to the host with .cpu() inside the prefill (a GPU sync and a pageable copy per
tensor). Measured on the Qwen3.6-35B recipe (same store): prefill 4.1k -> 2.7k tok/s at 33k tokens, -13% at 8.8k.
What: cuda/prompt_store.py Copier: each tensor is snapshotted on the compute stream (a fresh tensor, so later writes to
its source cannot race), copied to pinned host memory on a side stream (record_stream keeps the snapshot alive), and
the writer thread waits on the copy's event before saving. families/qwen4_exp/cuda/disk_points.py uses it.
Measured (35B, same change in its adapter): 33k prefill 2.7k -> 4.0k tok/s (cache off: 4.1k); restore tests unchanged
(a conversation evicted by 10 others reloads from disk and gives the same greedy reply).

diff --git a/src/tensorfold/cuda/prompt_store.py b/src/tensorfold/cuda/prompt_store.py
index d0d5c02..02f34e3 100644
--- a/src/tensorfold/cuda/prompt_store.py
+++ b/src/tensorfold/cuda/prompt_store.py
@@ -79,6 +79,36 @@ def ids_hash(ids) -> str:
     return hashlib.blake2b(np.asarray(ids, dtype=np.int32).tobytes(), digest_size=16).hexdigest()
 
 
+class Copier:
+    """A point's device tensors to pinned host memory without stopping the GPU (local patch 0008): each is first
+    snapshotted on the compute stream (later writes to its source cannot race the copy), then copied on a side stream;
+    ``done()`` is the event the writer waits on before it saves them."""
+
+    def __init__(self) -> None:
+        self.stream = torch.cuda.Stream() if torch.cuda.is_available() else None
+
+    def host(self, t: torch.Tensor, *, private: bool = False) -> torch.Tensor:
+        """``t`` on the host (``private``: ``t`` is already a fresh tensor nothing else writes)."""
+
+        if self.stream is None or not t.is_cuda:
+            return t.detach().cpu()
+        if not private:
+            t = t.clone()
+        self.stream.wait_stream(torch.cuda.current_stream())
+        with torch.cuda.stream(self.stream):
+            h = torch.empty(t.shape, dtype=t.dtype, pin_memory=True)
+            h.copy_(t, non_blocking=True)
+        t.record_stream(self.stream)                    # its memory is not reused before the copy ends
+        return h
+
+    def done(self):
+        if self.stream is None:
+            return None
+        event = torch.cuda.Event()
+        event.record(self.stream)
+        return event
+
+
